          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Recognition and Awards</strong><br>\nPeter Higgs's work was widely recognized in the scientific community. Despite the initial skepticism, the Higgs mechanism gradually gained acceptance as a pivotal element in the Standard Model. Over the years, Higgs received numerous awards and honors for his contributions, including the prestigious Nobel Prize in Physics in 2013.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Search for the Higgs Boson</strong><br>\nFor decades, the existence of the Higgs boson remained unconfirmed, making it one of the most elusive particles in physics. The search for the Higgs boson involved thousands of scientists worldwide and led to the development of the Large Hadron Collider, the world's largest and most powerful particle accelerator.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Confirmation of Theory</strong><br>\nThe discovery of the Higgs boson was announced on July 4, 2012, by scientists at CERN. This monumental finding confirmed Higgs's theoretical framework and was a testament to the predictive power of theoretical physics. It was a landmark moment for Higgs and the physics community.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
