          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Physics</strong><br>\nThe confirmation of the Higgs boson had a profound impact on the field of physics. It solidified the Standard Model, which is currently the best explanation for how the fundamental particles interact and govern the structure of matter in the universe. Higgs's work expanded our understanding of the universe and opened new avenues for scientific exploration.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Retirement</strong><br>\nAfter his retirement from active research, Peter Higgs became a notable figure in the scientific community. He continued to attend conferences and engage with physicists, providing insight into his work and its implications. Despite his fame, Higgs is known for his modesty and his preference for a quiet, private life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Future of Physics</strong><br>\nPeter Higgs will be remembered for his significant contribution to modern physics. The discovery of the Higgs boson is not the end but rather a new beginning for theoretical and experimental physics. Future research inspired by Higgs's work continues to probe deeper into the mysteries of the universe, such as dark matter and quantum gravity.</p>\n"
              },
